ace in  terms of how long you should wait before  you notify someone and i think the law  will help solve the problem but not  totally because the whole issue is this  cultural bias the fact that and we don't  know how many times they have not  notified others but if it's because of  the race that's a problem they need to  make sure they treat all of the victims  the same yeah absolutely lisa all right  former swat former detective veteran  your experience goes on and on but so  what are some of the procedures and  rules that you have seen about notifying  family when someone has been either  killed or died  departments do have protocols and  policies there's not a bill that  requires you to do it in a certain way  that just comes down to training and how  you're trained on your job in your  particular agency  agencies have it set up to where is you  make notification in a prompt and  courteous way in person with two  officers as soon as you find out who the  next of kin are a lot of times the news  media gets access to it faster than a  notification can be made because they're  having difficulty with the  identification so it's important yes  this bill is important because obviously  bridgeport connecticut definitely  dropped the ball right we'll see how  this bill affects how bridgeport  connecticut and maybe other cities  around the country go forward with  notifying next of kins that their loved  ones have been lost to them thank you  both when we come back the sarah  lawrence sex cult federal trial long  crimes adam classville reports as both  sides present opening statements in the  high-profile case of lawrence ray  welcome back to law and crime daily  opening statements are presented in  federal court as the accused sarah  lawrence college cult leader lawrence  ray stands trial on charges of abuse and  extortion the allegations date back to  2010 when former wall street trader  lawrence wray moved into his daughter's  on-campus housing at sarah lawrence  aft